P18-V01 active channel-event callback shutdown parity —
2026-10-22 21:56 UTC

Environment: macOS AArch64, Rust 1.85.0. Branch:
`phase/18-phase-18-compatibility-closure`. Java reference is RocketMQ 5.5.1,
commit `efa1be59d6fc747ad220f036c86030f05f0419f9`.

Source review found that Java `ChannelEventListener.onChannelActive` runs
synchronously on `NettyEventExecutor`; `NettyRemotingClient.shutdown()` waits
for that worker through `ServiceThread.shutdown()` for up to 90 seconds. Rust's
public async Active adapter had been canceled on shutdown. It now runs to
completion on its owned event worker, matching the synchronous Java callback
flow. `shutdown().await` still returns after the 90-second join bound if the
callback remains active; the worker can continue in background.

Code/test commit: `4248ce38 fix(remoting): drain active callbacks on shutdown`.
The slow-listener unit and scripted-peer tests now explicitly release the
callback and verify its completion; transport RPC continues while the observer
is slow.

Current-revision verification:
- `cargo test --offline --workspace --all-features --lib --quiet --locked` —
  PASS.
- Remoting library tests — PASS (140 tests).
- Remoting `tests/transport.rs` — PASS (107 tests).
- Core `tests/heartbeat.rs` — PASS (17 tests).
